# Hook scripts run under bash, and the context files they read are emitted as a
# JSON string. A CR that survives a Windows checkout ends up inside that string
# as a bare control character, which is not valid JSON. Normalise on the way in
# and check out LF everywhere so the hook sees the same bytes on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# PowerShell is happy with LF, but keep the intent explicit alongside the rest.
*.ps1  text eol=lf

*.png  binary
